{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 84cbe7b4f8a5d6d20efa5b89460049d316d31750, tree 6ed21113, on builder/nf8-witness-failure-page-20261117, all 4 artifacts, for request 2bd8f12d under my promise fe8369bf. This verdict names the one implementation: NF-8 (request 817a02ff, promise a5cf1c11, report `apps/room/page/test/witness-failure-page.mjs`, primary). Main d3896041 is the parent. The head carries out decision 58a0c09c.\n\n## What I read\n\n`witness-failure-page.mjs`:\n\n- `redact()` replaces every `artroom-invite:` token, whatever its value. It also replaces each value it is given.\n- `saveFailedPage()` reads the visible text of `body`, redacts it and writes `failure-page.txt` with flag `wx`. If redaction changed anything, it takes no screenshot and records why. Otherwise it takes a full-page screenshot with `[data-invitation]` masked. It catches every error and records only the error's name.\n\n`custody-witness.mjs`:\n\n- In hosted mode, `hostedPage` holds the Counter page, the evidence directory and the invitation as the one given secret.\n- A successful run clears `hostedPage` before it closes the page, so only a failed hosted run saves a page.\n- The catch block saves the page before it writes the private failure file. The run then fails as before.\n\n`scripts/test.mjs` adds the Node test to `nodeFiles`.\n\n## Security, first\n\n- **The screenshot.** The invitation goes into a `\u003ctextarea data-invitation\u003e` (`apps/counter/browser/main.ts:24`, filled at `custody-witness.mjs:178`). A field's value is not part of `innerText`, so the text check alone would not catch it. The screenshot mask names that exact selector, so the field is covered. The page also loads an invitation from `#artroom-invite:` in the address into the same field (main.ts:89). A page screenshot does not include the address bar.\n- **The text.** Any token that the page prints as text is replaced, and so is the exact invitation. If either appears, no screenshot is taken, so a token